course: dictionary
lesson: 10523
title: Typhoon: one storm, three names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are different names for the same thing in different places. «The same kind of storm is called a hurricane in the Atlantic, a typhoon in the north-west Pacific, near the Philippines and Japan, and a cyclone in the Indian Ocean.» The place names around the word are the clues.
explain: Read the clues around typhoon. The sentence says it is a storm, and it happens near the Philippines and Japan, so it must be a storm in the north-west Pacific. Storms in the Atlantic are called hurricanes, and storms in the Indian Ocean are called cyclones.
explain: Now check the meaning. A typhoon is a very strong storm with heavy rain and very fast winds. Put «a very strong storm» in place of typhoon in the sentence. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Hurricanes, typhoons and cyclones are all one kind of storm, called a tropical cyclone. The different names depend on which ocean the storm is in. So a story about a hurricane in the Atlantic is describing the same sort of storm.
fact: A typhoon is a very strong storm with heavy rain and very fast winds.
fact: Typhoons start over the warm western Pacific Ocean.
fact: The same kind of storm is called a hurricane in the Atlantic and a cyclone near Australia and India.
fact: Typhoons often hit countries such as the Philippines, Japan and China.
fact: When a typhoon is coming, listen to warnings, stay indoors, and keep away from windows and the sea.
exercise: «The same kind of storm is called a hurricane in the Atlantic, a typhoon in the north-west Pacific.» Where is a storm called a typhoon? | In the Atlantic | In the middle of a desert | In the Indian Ocean | *In the north-west Pacific, near Japan
exercise: A typhoon hits a town with 45 houses. 18 of the houses are damaged. How many houses are not damaged? | *27 | 33 | 63 | 28
exercise: A storm in the Atlantic is called a hurricane. What is the same kind of storm called near Japan? | *A typhoon | A drought | A tsunami | A blizzard
test: «Hurricanes, typhoons and cyclones are the same kind of storm.» What does this tell you? | Typhoons are never storms | They all happen in the Atlantic | *They are one kind of storm with different names in different oceans | Typhoons are only winds, with no rain
test: A radio warns that a typhoon is coming. What should you do? | Go out to find your friends | *Stay indoors and keep away from windows and the sea | Stand at the window to watch the storm | Go down to the beach to see the big waves
exam: Which word is the same kind of storm as a typhoon, the name used in the Atlantic? | Cyclone | *Hurricane | Tornado | Blizzard
